Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:27:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: only adjust sudogs for channels

Backport CL 847406, patch set 4, to Go 1.26. The upstream change is
still under review.

Restrict stack-pointer adjustment to channel sudogs. Semaphore and
sync.Cond sudogs do not point into goroutine stacks, and walking the
semaphore waiter list for every shrinking stack causes quadratic GC
work. Apply the corresponding single-waiter handling in goroutine
leak detection.

Preserve Microsoft Go's existing 32-bit g size in TestSizeof.

Upstream CL: https://go.dev/cl/847406
Upstream commit: f63d34a638baee4016360f9844da61ba16228e89
Upstream issues: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/81957 and
https://github.com/golang/go/issues/82189

